# This repository byte-compares generated output against committed golden files
# and against the tree in generated/. Git's autocrlf turns those files into CRLF
# on a Windows checkout while every generator here writes LF, so the comparison
# fails on a fresh clone for a reason that has nothing to do with the contract.
# That is not hypothetical: it failed on this machine the moment main was merged
# and checked out, and it would fail the same way on the hosted windows-latest
# runner the merge-gating tier is meant to run on.
#
# Everything the tooling reads or writes is therefore pinned to LF.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so Git must never touch line endings in them.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.pyd binary
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.lib binary
